Incorrect VLAN Assignment

Problem

PC7 and PC8, intended for the Management department, were accidentally assigned to VLAN 10 instead of VLAN 40.

Expected Configuration

Switch port Fa0/7: VLAN 40

Switch port Fa0/8: VLAN 40

PC7: 192.168.0.200/26

PC8: 192.168.0.201/26

Default gateway: 192.168.0.193

Symptoms

PC7 could communicate with PC8 while both were assigned to VLAN 10.

PC7 could not reach the intended Management gateway at 192.168.0.193.

PC7 could not reach the IT gateway at 192.168.0.1 because its IP address and default gateway were configured for the Management subnet.

Diagnosis

Used show vlan brief to inspect switch port assignments and identified that Fa0/7 and Fa0/8 belonged to VLAN 10 instead of VLAN 40.

Root Cause

Incorrect access VLAN configuration on the switch ports.

Resolution

Reassigned Fa0/7 and Fa0/8 to VLAN 40 using switchport access vlan 40.

Verification

Confirmed the correct VLAN membership with show vlan brief. Tested connectivity to the Management gateway, PC8, and a host in the IT VLAN.

Lesson Learned

Switch port VLAN assignment determines a device's Layer 2 broadcast domain. A correct IP address alone does not place a device in the correct VLAN. VLAN membership and IP subnet configuration must both be correct.
